{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quantile.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quantile.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quantile quantile","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quantile.md","fileName":"Quantile.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quantile","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Descriptive Health Statistics]] · [[Exploratory and Robust Data Analysis]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Descriptive Health Statistics","Exploratory and Robust Data Analysis","Percentile","Quantile-Based Grouping","Quantile-Quantile Plot","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quantile.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quantile.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quantile quantile","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quantile.md","fileName":"Quantile.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quantile","heading":"Quantile","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A quantile divides an ordered distribution according to a cumulative probability. Quartiles are quantiles at 0.25, 0.50, and 0.75, while arbitrary probability values yield corresponding [[Percentile|percentiles]].\n\nQuantiles are robust descriptions of position and useful inputs to [[Quantile-Based Grouping]]. Their calculation must specify how missing values are handled, because an unremoved missing value can prevent the estimate or silently change the analyzed subset.\n\nThe source presents a quantile as the inverse perspective on a cumulative distribution: a probability identifies the value below which that proportion of observations falls. This relationship makes quantiles useful both for distribution summaries and for constructing a [[Quantile-Quantile Plot]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Descriptive H